  "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
  "body": "**[Original report](https://bitbucket.org/agriggio/art/issues/259) by Alexander Korolev (Bitbucket: [ak-hpc](https://bitbucket.org/ak-hpc), GitHub: [ak-hpc](https://github.com/ak-hpc)).**\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nHello!\n\nI would like to have ISO, shutter speed, f-number and focal length values always on the screen in the editor, but in non-obtrusive way. I find quick info panel too obtrusive and inconvenient to use. I tried to add a line of text with this info to the navigator panel - two screenshots and patch attached. I kept it very simple \\(simple formatting, no other info like camera/lens model, etc.\\) and I like how it looks, but critique is welcomed.\n\nI also changed formatting a bit for exposure compensation to show plus sign for positive values, as I find it more informative.\n\nI used this particular order of values \\(iso, ss, f-number, focal length\\) because I find it more informative as well, even though it is not consistent with order used in other places \\(e.g. thumbnails tooltip or quick info panel\\).\n",
